     "question": "Explain the difference between primary, secondary and tertiary sectors with examples.",
     "marks": 3,
     "type": "short",
     "probability": "very-high",
     "answer": "The primary sector includes activities directly related to natural resources such as agriculture, forestry, fishing, and mining. For example, growing wheat or extracting minerals. The secondary sector involves processing and manufacturing of products, transforming raw materials into finished goods. Examples include making textiles from cotton or producing steel from iron ore. The tertiary sector provides services rather than goods, including transportation, banking, education, and healthcare. Examples include a hospital, school, or banking services. In India, the primary sector employs the maximum workforce while the tertiary sector contributes the most to GDP."
