     "question": "What is disguised unemployment? Explain with an example.",
     "marks": 3,
     "type": "short",
     "probability": "very-high",
     "answer": "Disguised unemployment occurs when more people are engaged in work than actually needed, with productivity remaining the same even if some workers are removed. It is commonly found in the agricultural sector in countries like India. For example, in a family of five members working on a small piece of land, if two members are removed, the total production remains the same. This shows that those two members were disguisedly unemployed as their marginal productivity was zero. This type of unemployment is hidden as people appear to be employed but are not making any significant contribution to production."
