     "probability": "high",
     "answer": "The organized sector follows government rules and regulations, while the unorganized sector does not. The organized sector includes enterprises registered under the Factories Act, Shops and Establishment Act, and other such laws. It provides job security, regular wages, paid leave, and social security benefits like provident fund, gratuity, and insurance. Examples include government departments, banks, and large industries. The unorganized sector includes small and scattered units that do not follow government regulations. It offers irregular employment, low wages, no job security, and no social security benefits. Examples include small shops, domestic workers, and agricultural laborers. The organized sector contributes about 65% of GDP but employs only 20% of workforce, while the unorganized sector contributes 35% of GDP but employs 80% of workforce."
