     "probability": "high",
     "answer": "Fair globalization refers to a form of globalization that creates opportunities for all and ensures that the benefits of growth are shared widely across society. It aims to make globalization more inclusive and equitable by addressing the negative impacts of globalization on certain groups and regions. The key principles of fair globalization include: 1) Inclusive growth: Ensuring that the benefits of globalization reach all sections of society, including the poor and marginalized. 2) Labor rights: Protecting workers' rights and ensuring fair working conditions across the globe. 3) Environmental sustainability: Promoting environmentally sustainable development practices that do not compromise the needs of future generations. 4) Democratic governance: Ensuring that decisions affecting global economic policies are made through inclusive and democratic processes. 5) Special treatment for developing countries: Providing special provisions and support to developing countries to help them benefit from globalization. Fair globalization requires reforms in international institutions like WTO, IMF, and World Bank to make them more responsive to the needs of developing countries. It also requires national governments to implement policies that ensure that the benefits of globalization are distributed equitably within their countries."
