     "probability": "high",
     "answer": "Quality marks like ISI, Agmark, and Hallmark play a crucial role in protecting consumer interests and ensuring product quality. Their significance for consumers can be understood through the following aspects: 1) Assurance of Quality: These marks indicate that a product has met certain quality standards set by the respective certification bodies. For example, ISI mark certifies that electrical products meet safety standards, Agmark certifies the quality of agricultural products, and Hallmark certifies the purity of gold and silver jewelry. This assurance helps consumers make informed purchasing decisions. 2) Protection Against Adulteration: Quality marks help protect consumers from adulterated or substandard products. For instance, Agmark ensures that food products are free from adulterants and meet prescribed quality standards, while Hallmark guarantees the purity of precious metals. 3) Safety: Certification marks like ISI ensure that products are safe for use. This is particularly important for electrical products, where poor quality can lead to accidents or hazards. 4) Value for Money: Quality marks help consumers get value for their money by ensuring that products meet minimum quality standards. This prevents consumers from being cheated with inferior products. 5) Standardization: These marks promote standardization in the market, making it easier for consumers to compare products and choose the best option. 6) Legal Protection: Products with quality marks are protected under various laws, giving consumers legal recourse in case of quality issues or defects. 7) Building Trust: Quality marks build trust between consumers and manufacturers, as they provide an independent verification of product quality. Overall, quality marks serve as a valuable tool for consumers, helping them make informed choices, ensuring product quality and safety, and protecting them from unfair trade practices."
