     "question": "Explain the concept of 'disguised unemployment' with a suitable example from the rural economy of India.",
     "marks": 3,
     "type": "short",
     "probability": "high",
     "answer": "Disguised unemployment refers to a situation where more people are engaged in work than actually required. If some workers are withdrawn from work, total output remains unaffected. In rural India, a common example is agriculture where a family of five members may cultivate their small land holding. Even if two members are withdrawn, the total production remains the same. This is because the work is divided among more people than necessary, leading to disguised unemployment. This type of unemployment is common in the primary sector of developing economies like India where surplus labor exists."
